# \"escaped\": 1
/* \"escaped\": 2 */
value: 3

----------------------------------------------------

[
	["comment", "# \\\"escaped\\\": 1\r"],
	["comment", "/* \\\"escaped\\\": 2 */"],
	["key", "value"], ["punctuation", ":"], ["number", "3"]
]

----------------------------------------------------

A backslash-escaped quote inside a comment does not start a string that would turn part of the comment into a key.
